1
0:00:00,300 --> 0:00:01,920
Hello everyone!

2
0:00:01,870 --> 0:00:05,340
In this video, I'll walk you through Analytivest.

3
0:00:05,340 --> 0:00:07,260
Invest with evidence.

4
0:00:07,260 --> 0:00:12,400
It's a data-led analysis app for Indian stocks and IPOs on

5
0:00:12,400 --> 0:00:13,470
NSE and BSE.

6
0:00:13,470 --> 0:00:16,160
First, the problems we all face.

7
0:00:16,160 --> 0:00:19,010
Then, how Analytivest solves them.

8
0:00:19,460 --> 0:00:21,900
Problem one: tips and hype.

9
0:00:21,850 --> 0:00:25,630
WhatsApp forwards, Telegram calls, grey market premium and

10
0:00:25,630 --> 0:00:29,090
subscription headlines push us into decisions without

11
0:00:29,090 --> 0:00:29,670
evidence.

12
0:00:29,670 --> 0:00:33,420
Problem two: data is scattered across annual reports,

13
0:00:33,420 --> 0:00:37,310
exchange filings, websites, and five-hundred-page RHPs.

14
0:00:37,310 --> 0:00:41,400
Problem three: most apps give one buy or sell rating, with

15
0:00:41,400 --> 0:00:43,590
no reasons, and lots of jargon.

16
0:00:43,590 --> 0:00:46,160
And problem four: hidden traps.

17
0:00:46,160 --> 0:00:49,840
Bonus issues distort EPS, some companies report in

18
0:00:49,840 --> 0:00:54,100
dollars, one-time gains inflate profits, and sometimes the

19
0:00:54,100 --> 0:00:55,640
data itself is wrong.

20
0:00:56,100 --> 0:00:59,280
Analytivest gives you three separate verdicts.

21
0:00:59,230 --> 0:01:02,050
Business quality: is the company strong?

22
0:01:02,050 --> 0:01:05,150
Financial risk: how vulnerable is it?

23
0:01:05,150 --> 0:01:07,960
And valuation: is the price reasonable?

24
0:01:07,960 --> 0:01:11,740
Every number shows its source, period and formula.

25
0:01:12,190 --> 0:01:15,560
Just type a company name or NSE symbol.

26
0:01:15,510 --> 0:01:19,870
If the same company is listed on NSE and BSE, it groups

27
0:01:19,870 --> 0:01:22,960
them together, with NSE as the default.

28
0:01:23,410 --> 0:01:25,320
Here is TCS.

29
0:01:25,270 --> 0:01:29,590
On top, the summary: strong fundamentals, with confidence

30
0:01:29,590 --> 0:01:31,260
and data completeness.

31
0:01:31,260 --> 0:01:34,340
Click why this score, to see what drove it.

32
0:01:34,340 --> 0:01:38,030
The fair-value range shows where today's price sits.

33
0:01:38,030 --> 0:01:42,220
Below, price and profit trends, plus positive factors and

34
0:01:42,220 --> 0:01:44,940
major risks, each backed by evidence.

35
0:01:45,410 --> 0:01:47,460
Every tab goes deeper.

36
0:01:47,410 --> 0:01:50,880
Financials, growth, debt and cash flow.

37
0:01:50,880 --> 0:01:54,740
Each chart has period selectors and a table view, and

38
0:01:54,740 --> 0:01:58,520
every jargon term has a simple explanation on hover.

39
0:01:58,980 --> 0:02:02,840
In valuation, you get multiples with their basis, the

40
0:02:02,840 --> 0:02:06,410
historical P/E band, and a DCF you can edit live.

41
0:02:06,360 --> 0:02:10,390
Change the growth rate, and the value and sensitivity grid

42
0:02:10,390 --> 0:02:11,570
update instantly.

43
0:02:11,570 --> 0:02:15,570
Peer comparison even catches bad provider data, and keeps

44
0:02:15,570 --> 0:02:17,180
it out of the averages.

45
0:02:17,640 --> 0:02:21,100
The risks tab is an automated red-flag system.

46
0:02:21,050 --> 0:02:24,770
For this sample company, it catches negative free cash

47
0:02:24,770 --> 0:02:28,140
flow, weak cash conversion, exceptional gains and

48
0:02:28,140 --> 0:02:31,580
dilution, each with evidence, severity and period.

49
0:02:31,580 --> 0:02:34,450
Signals to check, not accusations.

50
0:02:34,910 --> 0:02:36,900
And those hidden traps?

51
0:02:36,850 --> 0:02:41,460
HDFC Bank gets a bank-specific model, with its bonus issue

52
0:02:41,460 --> 0:02:42,180
adjusted.

53
0:02:42,180 --> 0:02:45,670
Infosys's dollar figures are converted to rupees.

54
0:02:45,670 --> 0:02:49,580
And demerger gains are excluded, so profit reflects the

55
0:02:49,580 --> 0:02:51,000
continuing business.

56
0:02:51,460 --> 0:02:53,800
Now, the IPO module.

57
0:02:53,750 --> 0:02:58,970
Upload the RHP or DRHP in any format: PDF, Word, even

58
0:02:58,970 --> 0:03:00,440
scanned images.

59
0:03:00,440 --> 0:03:04,380
Analytivest extracts the price band, fresh issue versus

60
0:03:04,380 --> 0:03:08,530
offer for sale, financials, peers and risks, and shows the

61
0:03:08,530 --> 0:03:10,530
exact page for every number.

62
0:03:10,530 --> 0:03:14,440
Then you get a clear suggestion: apply, borderline or

63
0:03:14,440 --> 0:03:15,840
skip, with reasons.

64
0:03:15,840 --> 0:03:19,960
Grey market premium and subscription numbers are ignored

65
0:03:19,960 --> 0:03:20,770
on purpose.

66
0:03:21,230 --> 0:03:24,880
You also get side-by-side comparison of up to five

67
0:03:24,880 --> 0:03:28,680
companies, a watchlist, saved snapshots, CSV and PDF

68
0:03:28,680 --> 0:03:32,180
export, dark mode, and a mobile-friendly layout.

69
0:03:32,590 --> 0:03:36,950
Remember, Analytivest is decision support, not investment

70
0:03:36,950 --> 0:03:37,490
advice.

71
0:03:37,440 --> 0:03:39,480
So that's Analytivest.

72
0:03:39,480 --> 0:03:41,400
Invest with evidence.

73
0:03:41,400 --> 0:03:44,520
Thanks for watching, and happy investing!
